                                        "entry_id": "4ccf3380-29eb-3903-9dac-dbcb8d11c541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of ancient Ausonia or the Ausonians."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f77288f0-6615-4005-b355-5df14c2f0df2",
                                                "sense_id": "8c178625-224e-3d2f-95c6-e99399c50eb7",
                                                "text": "Sometimes they marked the form of the silk-haired and graceful capella, with its wreathing horn and bright grey eye—which, still beneath Ausonian skies, recalls the eclogues of Maro, browsing half-way up the hills; and the grapes, already purple with the smiles of the deepening summer, glowed out from the arched festoons, which hung pendent from tree to tree."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f79ccb7-2ea4-40cd-9d59-bd088cecdd1a",
                                                "sense_id": "8c178625-224e-3d2f-95c6-e99399c50eb7",
                                                "text": "master of the glorious art of proud Ausonian song"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd319c57-4164-3cc0-9d08-4fa0a786fc9c",
                                        "entry_id": "4ccf3380-29eb-3903-9dac-dbcb8d11c541",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Italian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21ed0cc4-1792-477c-b8ac-a4e7dedd3b27",
                                                "sense_id": "cd319c57-4164-3cc0-9d08-4fa0a786fc9c",
                                                "text": "Or hollowing one hand against his ear, / To list a foot-fall, ere he saw / The wood-nymph, stay'd the Ausonian king to hear / Of wisdom and of law."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
